{"kind":"request","text":"MVP S1: create and seed the repo-in-ai room\n\nScope: the first data slice of the MVP plan (notes/2026-10-16-repo-in-ai-mvp-plan.md, section S1), placed by plan 032 section 2b. Create the user-test room on the dap-demo Worker with dap create, join the two coding agents and the checker by agent-key links, activate the change lane definition the plan names (change3.json or its current successor on main), seed the destination from a new examples/repo-in-ai/task-list/ directory, publish the rules, append the role actions, and write examples/repo-in-ai/runbook.md so that the whole setup is one script a person can rerun.\n\nChanges since the plan was written, which this slice follows instead of the plan's text: the Cloudflare freeze is over and rooms are created on dap-demo (namespace dap-demo, not artroom-demo); self-contained app install (M1, landed 40e37d85) is available, so the extension package installs by dap install rather than by hand; the 15-minute founding window applies to dap create (ruling a21306a8), so the runbook runs found, seat and first-key in one invocation.\n\nDone when, the plan's witnesses: the seed matches task-list/ byte for byte after git pull from the room's destination; each agent shows kind agent, role agent and the owner as controller in the membership summary; an agent's review-verdict is refused and the owner's accepted; every role keeps its earlier actions after the append. The runbook is the witness script, and its run on a scratch room is the evidence.\n\nNot before: J4 lands. The room created here is the one S2 to S9 use; name it in the runbook and in the note. Checker approves the exact head; gate passes; the planner creates the real room by running the runbook, as with the J4 rooms.","body":{"conditions":"Done when: the seed matches task-list/ byte for byte after git pull; each agent shows kind agent, role agent, owner as controller; an agent's review-verdict is refused and the owner's accepted; every role kee